CREATED:20260501T161641Z
DESCRIPTION:Co-presented with Cary\, NC • ADF-Commissioned World Premieres
  • ADF Debuts\nProgram: New works by Tracey Durbin\, Jabu Graybeal\, Cour
 tney Liu\, & Amanda K. Miller\nRunning time: 90 minutes\, including one i
 ntermission\nTickets: $30\nTickets are purchased through Duke University'
 s Box Office.\n\nThe Made in NC program features the world premiere of fo
 ur ADF-commissioned works by North Carolina artists. Tracey Durbin\, now 
 based in NC after 25 years as a central figure in Portland's dance scene\
 , continues to shape the state's artistic landscape through choreography\
 , teaching\, and collaborations with institutions such as the North Carol
 ina Museum of Art. Pittsboro native Jabu Graybeal\, an award-winning tap 
 artist who trained with the North Carolina Youth Tap Ensemble\, has perfo
 rmed with companies such as Caleb Teicher & Company and Michelle Dorrance
 \, appeared in Apple TV+'s Spirited\, and now shares his work with millio
 ns globally. He recently performed a tap duet with Kenji Igus on Netflix'
 s talent competition show Star Search. Courtney Liu\, Director-Choreograp
 her and Assistant Professor of Music Theatre at Elon University\, merges 
 Broadway experience with deep roots in NC's academic and performance comm
 unities. Amanda K. Miller\, founder of Pretty Ugly Dance Company and a fo
 rmer founding member of Ballet Frankfurt\, brings decades of internationa
 l experience to NC\, where she works as a choreographer\, opera director\
 , and educator. An encore performance will take place at Downtown Cary Pa
 rk on September 26 at 7:30 pm.\n_________\n\nADF offers a 20% discount to
  Duke employees and $20 tickets to Duke students (restrictions apply). To
  access your discount\, just log in with your Duke Net ID at tickets.duke
 .edu.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260501T161813Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T193000
