DESCRIPTION:<b>REGISTRATION</b>: <a href="https://duke.is/4/atw4" target="
 _blank">Click Here</a>\n\n<i>NOTE: Registration closes 24 hours before ev
 ent start. Please register ahead of the event. Registrants will receive Z
 oom information and related materials by email one week and within 24 hou
 rs before the event.</i>\n\nReserve your seat in the virtual Research Int
 egrity Roundtable <i>Mentorship and Research Integrity: Discussions for m
 entors and mentees</i> on June 24\, 2026 from 1:30pm - 3:00pm. Participan
 ts will learn about why good mentorship is important\, crucial components
  of mentorship in research\, and tips to combat insufficient mentorship f
 or mentors and mentees. Participants will discuss a case study related to
  a mentorship dilemma in small groups and as a large group.\n\nThis event
  is only open to current Duke faculty\, staff\, and students. Participati
 on in this event fulfills the <b>RCR-200</b> requirement for Faculty and 
 Staff\, the <b>200-level NSF RECR</b> requirement\, and the <b>715 RCR cr
 edit</b> for graduate students. Participants must attend for 60 minutes a
 nd participate in breakout room discussion to receive credit.\n\nFor more
  information on the NSF RECR training requirement please see the <a href=
 "https://myresearchpath.duke.edu/nsf-responsible-and-ethical-conduct-rese
 arch-recr-training" target="_blank">myRESEARCHpath page</a>.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260430T151310Z
